# DISABLED under PipeWire.
#
# This used to force ALSA's default device to card 1 to pick the analog codec
# over HDMI on the Legion. Under PipeWire that is now actively harmful: a
# `type hw` default makes ALSA clients grab the hardware device directly,
# bypassing PipeWire entirely, so pamixer/pavucontrol/bluetooth routing stop
# affecting them and the device gets locked against other apps.
#
# wireplumber picks the right sink by priority instead. If it still guesses
# wrong, set the default with `wpctl status` + `wpctl set-default <id>` rather
# than reinstating this file.
#
# pcm.!default {
#   type hw
#   card 1
# }
#
# ctl.!default {
#   type hw
#   card 1
# }
